# THE MEMBER'S WORK. Never tracked, so `git pull` never conflicts.
# The repo ships empty starters in starters/. code/workspace.py copies them into
# place once, and from then on these are the member's files alone. Without this
# split, the first update collides with a month of their work and they stop
# pulling, which quietly turns a living repo into a snapshot.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `context/` would also swallow
# starters/context/, and the starters would never ship.
/context/
/data/
/jobs/
/audit-report.md
/benchmark.md
/profile.md
/follow-ups.md

# Credentials, never
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
node_modules/
/cockpit/.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
